- **Type A (Broad/Exploratory)**: General topic queries ("what is diabetes", "chris pratt", "history of AI").
  - CORE = foundational defining facts. AUXILIARY = statistics, supplementary details.
  - Document must provide substantial coverage of at least ONE core aspect to qualify for 3+.
- **Type B (Specific/Closed)**: Queries requesting a specific answer ("release date of X", "who won the game", "net worth of Y").
  - CORE = the specific requested fact. Nothing else substitutes.
  - **HARD GATE**: Missing the specific answer = capped at 2/SM, regardless of how much related context is provided.
- **Type C (List/Multi-Part)**: Comparisons, multi-item requests, pros-and-cons ("X vs Y", "top 10 movies", "benefits and risks of Z").
  - CORE = coverage of all requested items/aspects.
  - **HARD GATE**: Covering <50% of requested items = capped at 2/SM.